==Ancient Greek==
[[File:Ὁ κύων.jpg|thumb|ὁ ποιμενῐκὸς κῠ́ων. ὁ κύων ὑλακτεῖ· βαύ, βαύ.|300px]]

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA|κύ˘ων}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|grc|ine-pro|*ḱwṓ|t=dog}}. Cognates include {{cog|la|canis}}, {{cog|sa|श्वन्|tr=śván}} and {{cog|ang|hund}} ({{cog|en|hound}}).<ref>{{R:grc:Beekes|811|κύων}}</ref> The final {{m|grc||-ν}} in the nominative singular which was absent in {{m|ine-pro|*ḱwṓ}} was restored in Greek by analogy to other forms in the paradigm.

====Noun====
{{grc-noun|κῠ́ων|κῠνός|m|g2=f|third}}

# a [[dog]]
# a [[bitch]]
# {{lb|grc|pejorative}} a [[bitch]] {{qualifier|used of women, to denote shamelessness or audacity}}
# an [[offensive]] [[person]]

